+## 9. Campaign-systems card — `UPGRADE: INFERENCE-ID-TAINT`
+
+**Problem.** Hash-pinned declared inputs and claim-parent DAGs catch stale
+files, but they need not catch a repeated semantic inference copied into a
+fresh report. The td8 repair supplies the exact control: the invalid inference
+“one flag implies no conjugate-series split” can survive even when all file
+hashes are fresh.
+
+**Smallest useful bounded implementation.** Add a stable inference ID plus
+scope predicates to every load-bearing derivation edge. Seed
+`ONE_FLAG_IMPLIES_NO_SERIES_SPLIT` as invalid. Register the two safe
+replacements separately: the `q>=2` weight branch and the `q=1` integral-
+arity branch. In memory, propagate taint through inference dependencies and
+run only four fixtures:
+
+1. an old td8 descendant using the invalid inference must fail;
+2. the repaired td8 proof must pass;
+3. the td12 exact B-charge proof must remain green; and
+4. an unrelated U2 ODE claim must remain green.
+
+Adopt only if all four outcomes are exact. Stop if history cannot link an
+inference without manual guessing or if either unrelated fixture is tainted.
+
+**Systems coverage.** Exact claim hashes preserve freshness and
+reproducibility; inference IDs reduce semantic retrieval cost and improve
+duplicate detection by fingerprinting object, quantifiers, mechanism, and
+scope. Tainted load-bearing claims are routed to a different model for repair,
+while unaffected work remains available, improving model utilization. The
+adapter parser rejects missing or unknown required IDs before execution.
+No AWS scheduling or cost change is needed. The operator/chat summary gains
+one line listing tainted descendants and the originating invalid inference,
+which is more actionable than a generic stale-state warning. This upgrade is
+bounded and does not authorize a canonical edit in this round.
