+## 8. Mathematical software acceleration
+
+Build `EXIT-PARTITION/v1`, a tiny exact integer/partition checker, before the
+next exit-budget theorem. Its input schema must distinguish physical flags,
+places carried by each flag, conjugate series, orbit blocks, `q`, pole versus
+cv type, area/integrality constraints, and per-exit weights. It minimizes the
+weight of the actual selected exit set; it must never infer flag count from
+series count. It validates accounting only conditional on source-provenanced
+typing and weight axioms; it does not prove those axioms. If the place-to-flag
+map, orbit partition, shared-suffix relation, or any weight premise is absent,
+its only legal result is `UNTYPED/NO_VERDICT`.
+
+The bounded acceptance suite is:
+
+1. reviewed td8 `q>=2` returns flag cost at least 3;
+2. reviewed td8 `q=1` rejects a lone weight-`3/2` flag and returns at least two
+   flags of total cost at least 4, hence full minimum 8;
+3. reviewed td12 B alternatives return exactly 8 versus at least 16;
+4. actual pole price returns 0; and
+5. a mutation using “one flag implies no series split” fails closed.
+
+This is a theorem-accounting accelerator, not a numerical book cap. It is
+desk-scale and warrants no AWS use.
